<body> <!-- NAV --><nav><div class="nav-inner"> <a href="https://marketingsignals.com" class="nav-logo"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," alt="Marketing Signals"></a><ul class="nav-links"><li><a href="#findings">Key Findings</a></li><li><a href="#table">Full Rankings</a></li><li><a href="#top">Top Performers</a></li><li><a href="#bottom">Bottom Performers</a></li><li><a href="#strategy">How to Improve</a></li></ul></div></nav> <!-- HERO SPLIT --><div class="hero-split"><div class="hero-photo"></div><div class="hero-text-side"> <span class="hero-pill">New Research — Spring 2026</span><h1 class="hero-title">Top UK Fashion &#038; Apparel<br><em>AI Visibility Index</em></h1><p style="font-size:17px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.65;">We tested 59 UK fashion &#038; apparel retailers across ChatGPT and Google AI to find out who&#8217;s winning in AI search, and the results are not what you&#8217;d expect.</p></div></div><div class="ms-bar"></div> <!-- INTRO — image bg with text overlay --><div class="img-bg-section"><div class="img-bg-inner"><p class="lede">An increasing number of online shoppers are asking AI for outfit ideas, gift inspiration, or where to buy specific items. But which of the leading fashion and apparel brands are being recommended the most by platforms such as ChatGPT, Perplexity and Gemini? We wanted to find out, which is why we built the UK Fashion and Apparel AI Visibility Index.</p><p>We pulled data on how often each retailer is mentioned and cited in AI-generated answers across ChatGPT and Google AI, layered in SEMrush citation data and then measured all of it relative to each retailer&#8217;s estimated UK organic traffic.</p><p>That last bit is the bit that matters. Why? Because the biggest fashion brands will naturally get more AI mentions than smaller rivals by dint of the fact that they&#8217;re more established. By dividing every signal by traffic, we strip out the &#8220;size effect&#8221; to get a much fairer picture of who&#8217;s actually visible in AI search relative to their audience. The retailers that came out on top in our study weren&#8217;t all household names, and the ones at the bottom might surprise you.</p></div></div><div class="ms-bar"></div> <!-- PULL QUOTE --><div class="pull-quote"><div class="pull-quote-text"> Some of the UK&#8217;s most popular fashion retailers are comparatively invisible when shoppers ask ChatGPT or Google AI for recommendations. Next attracts an estimated 21.6 million monthly visits yet scores just 1.6 in our index. Whistles, with a fraction of that audience, scores 24.8.</div></div> <!-- FULL TABLE --><div class="section" id="table"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Full Rankings</div><h2 class="section-h">All 59 Retailers, <em>Ranked</em></h2><p class="section-p">The full ranking of all 59 UK fashion &#038; apparel retailers, scored from most to least visible in AI answers relative to their UK traffic. Click any column header to re-sort.</p><div class="scroll-hint">← Swipe to see full table →</div><div id="table-wrap"><table id="rank-table"><thead><tr><th data-col="rank" class="sort-asc">Rank <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th style="width:48px;"></th><th data-col="domain">Domain <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th data-col="traffic">UK Traffic <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th data-col="chatgpt">ChatGPT <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th data-col="googleai">Google AI <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th data-col="semrush">SEMrush <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th data-col="index">AI Index <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th><th data-col="tier">Tier <span class="sort-icon">&#x2195;</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-rank="1" data-domain="harrods.com" data-traffic="1151422" data-chatgpt="1.15" data-googleai="7.85" data-semrush="100.0" data-index="36.33" data-tier="Top 10"><td class="tc">1</td><td class="td">harrods.com</td><td class="tt">1,151,42